IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Canada Disability Benefit Act (S.C. 2023, c. 17) and Canada Disability Benefit
-- Regulations (SOR/2025-35) -- THE NOUNS: records and choices only. No rules.
--
-- LAYER 1 (the law, objectively). Nothing here takes anyone's point of view.
-- Every other layer-1 module imports this one, so the same person, month and
-- decision are declared once. A field is named for the fact it states; the
-- genitive 's supplies "is" or "has", so no field starts with "is" or "has".
-- A field that a witness of ordinary competence could testify to belongs here;
-- whether that fact makes anyone eligible is a rule, and lives with its section.
--
-- Source text: the plain-text renderings deposited in the inputs, which are NOT the
-- official text (see SOURCE-LICENSE.md).

§ `Canada Disability Benefit -- the nouns`

§§ `Regulations s 1 -- release, and custody under a sentence (used by s 2(1)(d) and s 2(3))`

-- The four ways of release the definition of "release" names: "release from custody
-- on earned remission, at the expiry of a sentence, or on parole or statutory release
-- that has not been terminated or revoked".
DECLARE `Way of release` IS ONE OF
    `release on earned remission`
    `release at the expiry of the sentence`
    `release on parole`
    `release on statutory release`

-- One release: the day, the way, and whether a parole or a statutory release was
-- terminated or revoked (the definition leaves such a release out).
DECLARE `Release event` HAS
    `the day of the release`                                          IS A DATE
    `the way of the release`                                          IS A `Way of release`
    `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked`       IS A BOOLEAN

-- One term of custody: whether it is the kind that s 2(1)(d) is about, when it began,
-- and the release (if any) that ended it.
DECLARE `Custody under a sentence` HAS
    `the sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the first day in custody`                                        IS A DATE
    `the release that ended the custody`                              IS A MAYBE `Release event`

§§ `Regulations s 11 -- a suspension that the beneficiary asked for`

-- The day the suspension takes effect (s 11(2)) and, if payment has resumed, any day
-- in the month in which it resumed (s 11(5)).
DECLARE `Suspension at the beneficiary's request` HAS
    `the day the suspension took effect`                              IS A DATE
    `a day in the month payment resumed`                              IS A MAYBE DATE

§§ `Regulations s 1 -- the payment period`

-- "Payment period" means the period beginning on July 1 of a calendar year and ending
-- on June 30 of the following calendar year.
DECLARE `Payment period` HAS
    `the first day of the payment period`                             IS A DATE
    `the last day of the payment period`                              IS A DATE

§§ `Regulations s 2 -- the facts about a person for one month`

-- One person and one month. "Month" is held as any day in it. Where a criterion is
-- tested "for a month", the record holds the fact as it stands throughout that month
-- (fork F1 in NOTES.md). The three facts about a spouse or partner are taken as they
-- stood on the last day of the month before (the day section 6(1) uses for the same
-- spouse; fork F7).
DECLARE `Person facts for a month` HAS
    `the month asked about`                                           IS A DATE
    `date of birth`                                                   IS A DATE
    `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Canadian citizen`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `a permanent resident`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `a temporary resident`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `months resident in Canada immediately before the month`          IS A NUMBER
    `a protected person`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the custody under a sentence`                                    IS A MAYBE `Custody under a sentence`
    `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the suspension the beneficiary asked for`                        IS A MAYBE `Suspension at the beneficiary's request`

§§ `Regulations s 2.1 and the related provision SOR/2026-123 s 14 -- a payment after a certificate`

-- One payment of the benefit made to the person after they obtained a certificate
-- referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act.
DECLARE `Payment made after a certificate` HAS
    `the payment is an allocation`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was entitled to the payment`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of the payment rests on that certificate` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Regulations s 6 -- income, working income and the household`

-- "Working income" of an individual for a taxation year (s 6(7)): the amounts in
-- paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act
-- (borrowed, taken as one fact), plus five kinds of net business income that
-- the Regulations name.
DECLARE `Working income` HAS
    `amounts referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition working income in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER
    `net farming income`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `net fishing income`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `net professional income`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `net commission income`                                           IS A NUMBER
    `other net business income`                                       IS A NUMBER

-- One Consumer Price Index figure (s 6(6)): the all-items Consumer Price Index for
-- Canada, annual average, not seasonally adjusted, for one calendar year, as published
-- by Statistics Canada. The figures are inputs: this encoding contains none.
DECLARE `Consumer Price Index figure` HAS
    `the calendar year of the figure`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS A NUMBER

-- What s 6(1) needs to know about a beneficiary for one month. The incomes are for the
-- last taxation year that ended before the payment period began.
DECLARE `Income and household facts` HAS
    `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month that precedes the month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister waived the condition in subsection 2(4)`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `adjusted income without the income of a person who was the spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER
    `adjusted income as if the current spouse or partner had been the spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER
    `the beneficiary's own working income`                            IS A `Working income`
    `the working income of the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner` IS A `Working income`

§§ `Act s 9 -- claims against a benefit, and what the Act says about each`

DECLARE `Claim against a benefit` IS ONE OF
    `an operation of a law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency`
    `an assignment, charge, attachment or giving as security`
    `a retention by deduction, set-off or compensation under an Act of Parliament other than the Act`
    `a retention by deduction, set-off or compensation under the Act`
    `a garnishment for the purposes of the Family Orders and Agreements Enforcement Assistance Act`
    `any other claim`

DECLARE `Position of a benefit against a claim` IS ONE OF
    `the benefit is shielded from the claim`
    `section 9 does not shield the benefit from the claim`
    `the benefit is garnishable moneys`
    `the text does not say`

§§ `Act s 8 -- the party the Minister may make an agreement with`

DECLARE `Party to an agreement` IS ONE OF
    `a department or agency of the Government of Canada`
    `a department or agency of a province`
    `anyone else`

§§ `Regulations ss 17 to 20 and Act s 10.1 -- decisions, and how each may be challenged`

DECLARE `Decision of the Minister` IS ONE OF
    `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person`
    `a decision respecting the amount of a benefit that the person has received or will receive`
    `a decision imposing a penalty under section 35`
    `a decision on a request for reconsideration made under subsection 18(4)`
    `a decision on a request for an extension of time made under subsection 19(4)`
    `any other decision`

DECLARE `Way to challenge a decision` IS ONE OF
    `ask the Minister to reconsider it under section 18`
    `appeal it to the Social Security Tribunal`
    `the text states no route`

-- One request for reconsideration (ss 18 and 19): the decision it is about, when the person
-- was told of it in writing, when the request was made, how far the Minister extended the
-- time (if the Minister did), and what the request contains (s 18(3)).
DECLARE `Request for reconsideration` HAS
    `the decision`                                                    IS A `Decision of the Minister`
    `the person is dissatisfied with the decision`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision`      IS A DATE
    `the day the request was made`                                    IS A DATE
    `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days`        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the request is made in writing to the Minister`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the request gives the name and address of their representative`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Regulations s 19(3) -- the situations that can extend the 180 days`

DECLARE `Situation affecting a time limit` IS ONE OF
    `an emergency, if a state of emergency has been declared by a federal or provincial minister under federal or provincial law`
    `a natural or human-made disaster, such as a flood or fire`
    `a civil disturbance, such as a riot`
    `a disruption in public services, such as a strike`
    `a serious accident, injury or illness suffered by the person`
    `an emotional or mental distress suffered by the person, such as from a death in their family`
    `none of these`

§§ `Regulations ss 13 and 24 -- who is paid, and where a hearing is held`

DECLARE `Recipient of an amount owing on a death` IS ONE OF
    `the beneficiary's estate or succession or the beneficiary's heirs`
    `a person or agency designated by the Minister`

DECLARE `Place of a hearing` IS ONE OF
    `the city, town or village in which, or nearest to which, the appellant is ordinarily resident`
    `another place, or by audioconference or videoconference, with the appellant's written consent`

§§ `Regulations s 35 -- the violation behind a penalty`

DECLARE `Violation facts` HAS
    `knowingly made a false or misleading representation in relation to an application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made an application for, and received, a benefit knowing they were not eligible to receive it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person mistakenly believed the representation true or believed they were eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a prosecution for the act has been initiated against the person`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister became aware of the act on`                          IS A DATE
